/users/IlyaFinkelshteyn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaFinkelshteyn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaFinkelshteyn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-12-05T22:34:46Z","updated_at":"2017-12-05T22:34:46Z","body":"@ras0219-msft  that did not work as is. I was needed to add `System32` to the path. See https://github.com/Microsoft/vcpkg/pull/2309. \r\n\r\nHowever root cause is that path variable is broken at the point of calling that script. Here is what I see when replacing that command (directly in RDP session) with `echo %path%`. It [looks very short](https://ci.appveyor.com/project/IlyaFinkelshteyn/openlivewriter/build/0.6.2.10#L489):\r\n```\r\nC:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual Studio 14.0\\VC\\bin;C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Windows Kits\\8.1\\bin\\x86;;C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft SDKs\\Windows\\v10.0A\\bin\\NETFX 4.6.1 Tools;C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual Studio 14.0\\Common7\\tools;C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual Studio 14.0\\Common7\\ide;C:\\Program Files (x86)\\HTML Help Workshop;;C:\\Program Files (x86)\\MSBuild\\14.0\\bin\\;C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\Framework\\v4.0.30319\\;C:\\windows\\SysWow64;;;;;\r\n```\r\n\r\nI am not sure if **vcpkg** or something within **OpenLiveWriter** changing the `path` variablle. I cannot absolutely exclude that AppVeyor is changing something but this is not probable as we tested `path` before build command started. Also commands like [this](https://github.com/OpenLiveWriter/OpenLiveWriter/blob/master/src/unmanaged/OpenLiveWriter.Ribbon/OpenLiveWriter.Ribbon.vcxproj#L67) would not work if `path` broken before...\r\n\r\n@ras0219-msft if it works OK for you with another solution, then maybe this is not vcpkg issue.\r\n\r\nCC @jongalloway @willduff","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vcpkg/issues/comments/349464434/react